   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the town law and the public officers law, in relation to\nauthorizing the town justice of the town of Van Etten, county of Chemung, to\nbe a nonresident of such town",
    "basePrintNo": "S8551",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8551-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §23, Town L; amd §3, Pub Off L",
    "lawSection": "Town Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8551\n\nSPONSOR: O'MARA\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the town law and the public officers law, in relation to\nauthorizing the town justice of the town of Van Etten, county of\nChemung, to be a nonresident of such town\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to authorize the town justice of the Town of\nVan Etten, located in Chemung County, to be a nonresident of the town.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Amends Section 23 of the Town Law by adding a new subdivision\n35, which states that in the Town of Van Etten, Chemung County, the\nperson performing the function of Town Justice, need not be an elector\nof the town.\n\nSection 2: Amends Section 3 of the Public Officers Law by adding a new\nsubdivision 72.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation was requested by the town of Van Etten, county of\nChemung, pursuant to a resolution unanimously passed by the town board\nof Van Etten adopting Resolution Number 2022-20 on February 10, 2022.\n\nThere are no residents of the town who are ready, willing or able to\nserve as Town Justice. This legislation is therefore necessary to ensure\nthat the position can be filled by someone who is qualified and able to\nserve in this vital position.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n New bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
